CSVReminderColumns = Optional: a text column and a due date column to add a reminder to the todo, chosen when importing.
ReminderLabelColumn = Reminder text column
ReminderLabelColumnHelp = The text of this column becomes the label of a "To do" reminder event linked to the opportunity. It shows in the todo of the people assigned to the opportunity, or in yours when nobody is. Without text, the reminder is named "Reminder: First name Last name". "None", "-" or "I don't know" count as an empty cell.
ReminderDateColumn = Reminder due date column
ReminderDateColumnHelp = Due date (end date) of the reminder, as DD/MM/YYYY or YYYY-MM-DD, optionally followed by a time (14:30 or 14h30); without a time, 9:00. The reminder starts when imported. A missing or unreadable due date gives a reminder without due date, the value of the file ("3-6 months"…) is kept in its note. A past due date gives a late reminder, without notification.
ImportRemindersCreated = %s reminders added to the todo.
ImportRemindersWithoutText = %s reminders created without text, labelled "Reminder: First name Last name".
ImportRemindersWithoutDueDate = %s reminders created without due date: missing or unreadable date (accepted formats: DD/MM/YYYY or YYYY-MM-DD, time optional). The value of the file is kept in the note of the reminder.
ImportRemindersOverdue = %s reminders created with a due date already past: they are late in the todo, without notification.
ImportReminderDueDateAsWritten = Due date written in the import file: %s
ImportReminderErrors = %s reminders could not be saved.
CSVNoteColumn = Optional: a column of notes from 0 to 10 giving the probability of the opportunity (1 = 10%), chosen when importing.
NoteColumn = Note column (probability)
NoteColumnHelp = Note from 0 to 10 turned into the probability of the opportunity: 1 = 10%, 2 = 20%… 10 = 100% (2.5 = 25%). The opportunity also gets the matching status of the dictionary (prospection, qualification…). An empty cell leaves the row without probability. When it is the "Note" column expected by the import, a note no longer fills the description; a text still does.
ImportNotesInvalid = %s notes not used: unreadable value or out of 0 to 10.
