SepaMandateCheckTitle = SEPA mandate check
SepaMandateRuleIntro = This page tells, bank account by bank account, what will keep a SEPA direct debit from leaving correctly. It changes nothing: each row links to the bank accounts tab of the third party to fix it.
SepaMandateRuleFallback = With your Dolibarr version (%s), the signature date written in the file is the mandate signature date, or the creation date of the bank account when there is none.
SepaMandateRuleNofallback = Warning: with your Dolibarr version (%s), when a direct debit request designates a given bank account, the file takes the mandate signature date with no fallback. When it is not filled in, the date goes out empty and the bank rejects the file, unless the Dolibarr fix #42020 is installed.
SepaMandateRuleUncertain = With your Dolibarr version (%s), the Dolibarr fix #42020 may not be included: a bank account designated by a request and without a mandate signature date is therefore reported as blocking, to be safe.
SepaMandateCheckedAccounts = Bank accounts checked
SepaMandateAccountsBlocking = Bank accounts with a blocking issue
SepaMandateAccountsWarning = Bank accounts to watch
SepaMandateFailingRequests = Pending requests that will fail
SepaMandateFailingRequestsHint = out of all the pending direct debit requests
SepaMandateThirdpartiesInError = Third parties without a usable bank account
SepaMandateSeverity = Severity
SepaMandateSeverityBlocking = Blocking
SepaMandateSeverityWarning = To watch
SepaMandateSeverityOk = Correct
SepaMandateFilterAll = All rows
SepaMandateFilterIssues = Blocking or to watch
SepaMandateFilterPending = Only bank accounts with a pending request
SepaMandateBankAccount = Bank account
SepaMandateRum = UMR
SepaMandateDateRum = Mandate signature date
SepaMandateDateWritten = Date written in the file
SepaMandatePendingRequests = Pending requests
SepaMandateIssues = What to fix
SepaMandateNone = No bank account matches these filters.
SepaMandateNoUsableAccount = No usable bank account
SepaMandateNoLabel = Unnamed bank account
SepaMandateNoIban = No IBAN
SepaMandateNoIssue = Nothing to report
SepaMandateDateEmpty = empty
SepaMandateDateReasonMandate = mandate signature date
SepaMandateDateReasonCreation = creation date of the bank account, for lack of a signature date
SepaMandateDateReasonEmpty = no date to write
SepaMandateDateReasonEmptyunlessfix = empty, unless the Dolibarr fix #42020 is installed
SepaMandateFix = Fix
SepaMandateFixOnThirdparty = Open the bank accounts tab of the third party
SepaMandateReadOnlyNote = IBANs are never shown in full. The check follows the rules Dolibarr applies when it creates a direct debit order: a validated, unpaid invoice with a pending request.
SepaMandateIssueDateMissingEmpty = Mandate signature date missing. This bank account is designated by a pending request: with Dolibarr %s, the file will leave with an empty signature date and the bank will reject it, unless the Dolibarr fix #42020 is installed. Fill in the mandate signature date on the bank account.
SepaMandateIssueDateMissingUncertain = Mandate signature date missing. This bank account is designated by a pending request: if your Dolibarr version (%s) does not include the fix #42020, the file will leave with an empty signature date and the bank will reject it. Fill in the mandate signature date on the bank account.
SepaMandateIssueDateMissingNoDate = Mandate signature date missing, and the bank account has no creation date: the file will leave with an empty signature date. Fill in the mandate signature date on the bank account.
SepaMandateIssueDateMissingFallback = Mandate signature date missing: Dolibarr will write the creation date of the bank account instead (%s), which is not the day the customer signed. Fill in the actual signature date.
SepaMandateIssueDateFuture = Mandate signature date in the future (%s): a direct debit cannot rely on a mandate not signed yet, the bank will reject the line. Correct the signature date.
SepaMandateIssueRumMissing = Unique mandate reference (UMR) missing: Dolibarr will make one up, which will not match the mandate signed by the customer. Copy the UMR of the signed mandate.
SepaMandateIssueRumDuplicate = Same mandate reference (UMR) as %s: each mandate needs its own reference, or the bank mixes them up. Correct the UMR of one of the bank accounts.
SepaMandateIssueIbanMissing = IBAN missing: no direct debit can leave on this bank account. Copy the IBAN from the signed mandate.
SepaMandateIssueIbanInvalid = Invalid IBAN (its check digits do not match): Dolibarr will leave the invoice out of the direct debit file. Copy the IBAN from the signed mandate.
SepaMandateIssueBicMissing = BIC missing: Dolibarr will leave the invoice out of the direct debit file. Fill in the BIC of the customer's bank.
SepaMandateIssueBicInvalid = Malformed BIC (%s): it has 8 or 11 characters, letters and digits, no space. Dolibarr will leave the invoice out of the direct debit file.
SepaMandateIssueDuplicateDefault = This third party has several default bank accounts: Dolibarr will stop the creation of the direct debit order. Keep only one as default.
SepaMandateIssueDesignatedInactive = This bank account is disabled, but a pending request designates it: Dolibarr will still debit this account. Enable it again if it is right, otherwise delete the request and make it again on the right bank account.
SepaMandateIssueDesignatedMissing = The request of invoice %s designates a bank account that no longer exists: Dolibarr will debit the default bank account of the third party instead. Check it is the right account.
SepaMandateIssueNoAccount = %s pending direct debit request(s), but no bank account is recorded for this third party: nothing can be debited. Add the bank account of the signed mandate.
SepaMandateIssueNoDefault = %s pending direct debit request(s), but no bank account is set as default: Dolibarr will not put these invoices in the file. Set the bank account of the mandate as default.

